From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sinful1992 <sinful1992@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 10:51:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Only label Dolby Vision in HLS for clients that declared DOVI
 support

A copied DV profile 8.x stream got SUPPLEMENTAL-CODECS="dvh1.08.06/db1p"
on its variant regardless of what the client asked for. The master
playlist also carries an H.264 SDR entrance at the same BANDWIDTH.
ExoPlayer (Jellyfin Android TV 0.20.0-hero.31 on a Sony KD-65X75WL)
parses the tag as video/dolby-vision and picks the H.264 entrance, so an
audio-only transcode (TrueHD -> AAC) became a full 4K software HEVC
decode + h264_vaapi encode at ~1.0x realtime. The same request for an
HDR10 file without DV picks the hvc1 variant and copies video.

Apply the rule the P5 variant above already uses: emit the DV label only
when the request's range types include a DOVI type. The video is still
copied untouched; only the playlist label changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Jellyfin.Api/Helpers/DynamicHlsHelper.cs | 9 ++++++++-
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/Jellyfin.Api/Helpers/DynamicHlsHelper.cs b/Jellyfin.Api/Helpers/DynamicHlsHelper.cs
index 4995d37f4b..62b389f24c 100644
--- a/Jellyfin.Api/Helpers/DynamicHlsHelper.cs
+++ b/Jellyfin.Api/Helpers/DynamicHlsHelper.cs
@@ -538,7 +538,14 @@ public class DynamicHlsHelper
 
         if (EncodingHelper.IsDovi(state.VideoStream) && !_encodingHelper.IsDoviRemoved(state))
         {
-            AppendDvString();
+            // Only label Dovi for clients that explicitly declared DOVI support, same rule as the P5 variant above.
+            // ExoPlayer parses the tag as video/dolby-vision, may only reach it through a decoder fallback, and then
+            // picks the same-BANDWIDTH H.264 SDR entrance instead: a full re-encode of a stream it could have copied.
+            if (state.GetRequestedRangeTypes(state.VideoStream.Codec)
+                .Any(rangeType => rangeType.StartsWith("DOVI", StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)))
+            {
+                AppendDvString();
+            }
         }
         else if (EncodingHelper.IsHdr10Plus(state.VideoStream) && !_encodingHelper.IsHdr10PlusRemoved(state))
         {
